        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(doctor): preserve allowlist entries for version-bound runtime plugins during stale config scan",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nWhen a previously bundled `@openclaw/codex` plugin is externalized to an npm package, `doctor --fix` silently removes `\"codex\"` from `plugins.allow` during the first run after upgrade. The allowlist entry is pruned because `plugins.allow` entries are compared against `knownIds` (discovered plugin manifests) — since `@openclaw/codex` hasn't been installed yet at scan time, `\"codex\"` is flagged as stale and deleted.\r\n\r\nReported as issue #107226.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nThe stateful repair sequencing at `src/commands/doctor/repair-sequencing.ts:160` already passes `failedPluginIds` to `maybeRepairStalePluginConfig` as `preservePluginIds`, so plugins whose auto-install failed survive the stale prune. However, codex in `plugins.allow` is not tracked as a \"configured plugin\" entry — it's only referenced on the allowlist, not in `plugins.entries`. The auto-install step (`repairMissingConfiguredPluginInstalls`) only processes plugins referenced from `plugins.entries` or agent harness configurations, so `plugins.allow`-only entries are never in `failedPluginIds`.\r\n\r\nThe fix adds `VERSION_BOUND_RUNTIME_PLUGIN_IDS` (currently `new Set([\"codex\"])`) to the `preservePluginIds` spread at the call site. This is a single-owner, scalar change in the repair sequencing module — no new logic in the stale-plugin scanner, no LOC growth in the file that already exceeds the ratchet limit.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nTransparent — `plugins.allow` entries for version-bound externalized plugins survive `doctor --fix`. No configuration change needed.\r\n\r\n## Behavior Matrix\r\n\r\n| Scenario | Before | After | Changed? |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| `plugins.allow: [\"codex\"]` on first post-upgrade `doctor --fix` | `\"codex\"` removed (silent allowlist drop) | `\"codex\"` preserved (survives until release backfill install) | ✅ Fix |\r\n| `plugins.allow: [\"codex\"]` after `@openclaw/codex` is installed | `\"codex\"` kept (knownIds match) | `\"codex\"` kept (knownIds match) | ❌ No |\r\n| Non-version-bound stale plugin entry (e.g., retired channel) | Removed | Removed | ❌ No |\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n**Real environment tested**: Linux x86_64, Node v24.18.0, branch `fix/preserve-allowlist-version-bound-107226`.\r\n\r\n**Relevant code path**:\r\n\r\n`src/commands/doctor/repair-sequencing.ts:160`:\r\n```ts\r\npreservePluginIds: [...failedPluginIds, ...VERSION_BOUND_RUNTIME_PLUGIN_IDS],\r\n```\r\n\r\n`VERSION_BOUND_RUNTIME_PLUGIN_IDS` is exported from `missing-configured-plugin-install.ts` as `new Set([\"codex\"])`.\r\n\r\n**What was not tested**: Full `v2026.6.11 → v2026.7.1` end-to-end upgrade with a real gateway restart and Codex agent turn. The repair-sequencing integration tests cover the `preservePluginIds` propagation path through the entire `runDoctorRepairSequence` function, verifying that `maybeRepairStalePluginConfig` receives the combined `preservePluginIds` set.\r\n",
        "branch": "fix/preserve-allowlist-version-bound-107226-clean",
